-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
UNDERLYING DATA
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source records are United States Food and Drug Administration public
records. As works of the U.S. federal government they are not subject to
copyright protection in the United States (17 U.S.C. Sec. 105). The CC BY 4.0
license above applies to this project's ontology, code, transformations, and
the compiled graph as an original selection and arrangement -- not to the
underlying FDA facts.

The U.S. Food and Drug Administration does not endorse this project. FDA logos
and insignia are not used. Nothing here is FDA guidance, and nothing here
should be read as implying FDA review or approval.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
NO WARRANTY
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. This graph is intended for
research and education. It is not regulatory advice, not medical advice, and
not a substitute for consulting qualified regulatory professionals or primary
FDA sources.

Adverse event counts in this graph reflect reporting behavior and market
exposure, not device failure rates. The graph contains no utilization
denominators. Counts must not be presented as rates, and FDA does not verify
that a reported device caused a reported event.
